<VI _name="lvdqmh_btnpos.vi" description="READ-ONLY. Computes the SCREEN position of a front-panel control\2C so an OS-level mouse click can be aimed at it.\0A\0AWHY THIS EXISTS. Delacor's event dialog OK button has Mechanical Action 4\2C Latch When Released\2C and LabVIEW refuses Value and Value (Signaling) on a latched boolean - Error 1193. VI Server therefore cannot press it at all\2C and the only remaining route is a synthesised click. Aiming that click at coordinates read off a screenshot would be guesswork\3B these come from the panel itself.\0A\0ATHE ARITHMETIC. Front Panel Window\3APanel Bounds gives the panel AREA in screen coordinates. A control's Position is relative to the panel's own origin\2C and Front Panel Window\3AOrigin is how far that origin has been scrolled\2C so the control's screen position is PanelBounds.Left + (Position.Left - Origin.x)\2C plus half its width to land in the middle. The scroll term matters\3A this dialog is taller than its window and does scroll.\0A\0AThe label is returned alongside so the caller can prove the coordinates belong to the control it meant.">
